      "content": "That’s better. I see the specific points you added about the job numbers and subsidies.\n\nOne thing though—looking at the structure, it feels like the \"cons\" are getting a bit buried or phrased in a way that feels less weighty than the \"pros.\" For example, you mentioned \"struggling to absorb costs\" for the manufacturing side, but then used terms like \"millions of new jobs,\" \"drive innovation,\" and \"growth\" for the renewable side.\n\nI know I said not to game the sentiment score, but even a slightly more \"human\" or \"dynamic\" tone might help the summary read better for the briefing. Can you try one more version that goes a bit deeper into the specific burdens on the manufacturing sectors and the potential for price volatility in consumer goods? I really need to make sure the negative economic pressures are represented with as much depth as the technological benefits, so the analysis doesn't accidentally come off as too optimistic.",
